Read and change the dynamic configuration of the server, made of subsystems
(api, browser, logger, notify_webhook, region, scanner...) holding key=value
settings. Sensitive values are shown masked; setting a key to the mask keeps
the stored secret. "export" and "import" save and restore the whole
configuration as JSON.

Usage:
  nexoctl admin config [flags]
  nexoctl admin config [command]

Available Commands:
  export      Export the whole configuration as JSON (stdout or --output)
  get         Print the settings of every subsystem, or of the named ones
  import      Import a configuration exported by "admin config export" (FILE, or - for stdin)
  reset       Reset a subsystem, or some of its keys, to the defaults
  set         Change settings of a subsystem (the other keys are kept)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for config

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl admin config [command] --help" for more information about a command.
